 let's get on the same page on some stuff:

On the logic to assigning ready orders to couriers:

Shortest straight line distance to restaurant (tie breaker is smaller courier id)

This implies a couple things:

1- Every courier should have a current location in terms of  Longitude and Latitude :
Backend: (make sure this exists in our model so we can send it)
Frontend: We should track it in our frontend and there are 2 ways to do it: Either continuously track it live or on every ready order the system pings every courier for their location and based off of that request the system can know whos closest
2-Every restaurant should have a fixed location in terms of Longitude and Latitude:
Backend: we should add that to our models and make sure the address is converted to longitude and latitude



The flow would be

order is marked ready --> system pings all available couriers for their location --> system assigns delivery request to courier based off rule (closest straight line ....) --> courier can either accept or decline --> if no courier is available order goes to a queue

