PRC UC
1- Compute order fare (Nadine)

ID:
UC-PRC-01
Title:
Compute order fare
Description:
The total fixed fare of each order is calculated and recorded in the ledger. At checkout, as part of Place Order, PRC computes totalFare = SUM(unit price × quantity) + deliveryFee + serviceFee + smallOrderSurcharge, where the surcharge applies only when the subtotal is below the smallOrderThreshold. All values other than the order lines must come from the configuration file. PRC will record this amount as the order’s billing record when the order is placed (the total amount that the customer pays).


Primary Actor:
Customer
Preconditions:
A customer is logged in
The customer has selected items from an open restaurant
The configuration file contains : serviceFee, deliveryFee, smallOrderSurcharge, smallOrderThreshold
Postconditions:
The customer has seen the total fare
The placed order has a billing record holding its unit prices, subtotal, delivery fee, service fee, surcharge and total
No ledger entry exists yet
Inputs:
Order lines (menu item, unit price, quantity)
The pricing values (serviceFee, deliveryFee, smallOrderSurcharge, smallOrderThreshold)
Outputs:
Total itemized fare (subtotal, delivery fee, service fee, surcharge, total)
One billing record
One output console line (DASH)
Main Success Scenario:










2- Record order fare (Nadine)

ID:
UC-PRC-02
Title:
View order summary
Description:
When the order reaches a final state (Delivered | Rejected | Cancelled), PRC adds one ledger entry with that state, the order's timestamps and its total charge:
if delivered → total billing amount
if cancelled or rejected → 0$

Note that the total order fare is never recomputed, so an order's total cannot change.
